      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`tool_result.content` currently accepts thinking, tool-use and nested tool-result blocks, but the converter has no branch for them. The request continues with those blocks silently removed.\n\nReject unsupported nested types during protocol validation. Keep the existing text, image, tool_reference and search_result forms, and leave top-level assistant history unchanged.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nThe new rejection cases fail on base and pass with the fix. The existing focused tool-result/reference conversion tests also pass, including search-result flattening and mixed-content order. Actual protocol and serving modules were loaded in a disposable CPU environment. Focused lint/formatting pass.\n\nPrepared with Codex assistance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39988769619](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39988769619)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39988769493](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39988769493)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39988769516](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39988769516)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
